🛠️ Tools and Technologies Used
    ODK Collect App: For mobile-based field data collection with customizable forms.
    Microsoft Excel & Google Sheets: For data management and basic analysis.
    Google Drive & Email: For secure cloud-based storage and sharing.
    ODK Converter: To convert excel data to machine redable format.
    Google My Maps: For publishing and visualizing field data with geospatial insights.


📋 Workflow and Steps

Design & Deploy Survey Forms in ODK Collect
  Created structured, custom forms using ODK’s XLSForm format.
      Deployed forms on mobile devices using the ODK Collect app.
      (Sample form and design guide available in the Forms/ directory)

Collect Field Data with ODK Collect
  Used mobile devices to gather field data, including geotagged locations and images.
  (Raw data examples are available in the Data/Raw_Data/ folder)

Process & Export Data
  Exported raw ODK data using ODK Converter.
  Processed the data into CSV/Excel formats for easier analysis.

Visualize Data with Google My Maps
  Uploaded processed data to Google My Maps for interactive web visualization.
  Customized maps with geotagged images and filters for better insights.

Enhance Maps with Geotagged Images
  Added images with geospatial tags and location-based keywords to enrich the visualization.


💡 Key Learnings
  Mobile-based surveys simplify field data collection and enhance accuracy.
  Integrating ODK Collect with Google Sheets and My Maps creates a cost-effective GIS solution.
  Geotagging images provides rich spatial insights and improves map usability.






